    "rationale": "The four shapes of the entity-operation executor, one per item, against the SAME prior scope (one product, one customer). Reasoned from the switch: [0] 'clear' -> finalEntities [] outright, prior discarded, entity_op_applied 'clear'. [1] 'replace_combine' with a current PRODUCT -> the prior product shares product_scope and is evicted, the prior customer sits on order_scope and is KEPT; scope_exclusive_applied false. [2] scope_exclusive true WITH a current entity -> keptPrior is emptied outright, so the customer goes too and scope_exclusive_applied is true. [3] scope_exclusive true with NO current entity -> 'restrict to only nothing' is meaningless, so prior is kept whole and exclusive_ignored_no_current marks it. Domain is master_products throughout, whose blocklist drops 'customer' - so items 1 and 3 also show entities_filtered true with broaden_dropped naming the customer.",
